{"step_index":93,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T11:06:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-01T16:36:15+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-01T16:36:26+05:30\nThe search for \"Mac Mini M4 Pro 48GB 512GB configuration available or forced 1TB Apple store\" returned the following summary:\nThe **Mac Mini M4 Pro** allows for flexible configuration, and you are **not forced to upgrade to 1TB of storage** when selecting 48GB of unified memory[1][2].\n\nYou can configure the Mac Mini M4 Pro with **48GB of unified memory and the base 512GB SSD** through the official Apple Store's \"Configure to Order\" (CTO) options[3][2]. \n\n### Key Details:\n*   **Customization:** While retail stores often stock pre-configured base models (which may only come in specific standard variations), the **Apple Store online** provides the option to customize your Mac Mini[3][4]. You can mix and match memory and storage tiers within the limits allowed for the M4 Pro chip[3].\n*   **Availability:** Since this is a custom configuration (CTO), it may not always be available for immediate pickup at a physical Apple Store. You may need to order it online, and it will be assembled and shipped to you[5][4].\n*   **Third-Party Retailers:** Some third-party authorized resellers or distributors may list the specific 48GB/512GB configuration if they have imported or customized stock, but for the most direct and reliable purchasing path, the Apple website is the standard route[1][2]. \n\nIf you are using the Apple Store online, simply select the M4 Pro model and use the configuration menu to increase the memory to 48GB while leaving the storage at 512GB[3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [dotcomstores.in](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEHJUKsvcHsixluWuIP84kFF1eGc0kvmeE982DKLMBTwxfnC1yNIpDSg3uZB0iMCVA9ffq3zZIdXxthEam2-UiYH-JzMinplxh8Gn1cxWytv_p4rhPiVVjpGtqUzjOu4YXkcoVMXDQWR5C_ghPVJRsd2k_vXNN_xKFExi-sJaLenhBUCfS50NjkSvSuXGAf_VjP69s-xiQf0vEwkf8-GKRoZkK